meta {
  name: Crawl jobs
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/jobs/crawl/{{companyId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Crawl the company's website for open jobs with the AI provider (OpenAI) and create them. Set `companyId` to an id from **List companies**.

  Starts at the company's `websiteUrl`, finds the careers page through `/sitemap.xml`, navigation and footer, then extracts each job listing from its own page in a strict output format. Only pages on the company's domain (and subdomains) are followed; job boards are ignored.

  Jobs that already exist (same `sourceUrl` or `externalId`), job pages that fail to load and invalid AI results are skipped. `locationId` and `skills` stay empty.

  - 201: Created - the new jobs, shaped like job list items
  - 400: the company has no `websiteUrl`
  - 404: unknown company
  - 422: AI response hit the output token limit
  - 502: the website or the AI request failed
  - 401: run Login
}
